  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Big Box on the Shelf",
    "overview": "The game is the box it came in. The title screen is a 1997 big-box PC game front: box black, a silver extruded italic logo, a die-cut window showing the live city, and a hazard-yellow starburst price sticker that is the PLAY button. Pressing it grows the window to full screen, so the box opens into the game. The city is the foldout street map come alive: uncoated cream paper, ink casings on every road and roof, district roof tints, a grid of letters and numbers printed in the sea. HUD pieces are stickers slapped onto the box; pause is the printed manual, a two-page spread with keycaps and a map key.\n\nEverything is printed flat with ink outlines. Depth comes from print objects sitting on one another (a sticker on a box, a manual over the map), never from light. The system refuses dark glass panels over a neon arcade, scanlines, glow, CRT effects and emoji.\n\nMotion has three verbs. Stickers slap on (fast scale-down from 1.12 with a slight rotation, exponential ease-out). Banners slam in once and leave. The box window opens. Nothing loops for decoration.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Box black, silver-embossed italic display type, hazard-yellow sticker accents.",
      "Uncoated map-paper cream carrying map inks: route red, water blue, park green, district tints.",
      "Ink outlines (1.5 to 2px) on every printed object, in DOM and canvas alike.",
      "Condensed manual text with tabular numerals for every number on screen.",
      "Stickers sit slightly off-square (rotated -0.6deg to 8deg); print never sits perfectly true."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Sticker Rule",
        "body": "Hazard yellow is the only accent on any surface. If two things on screen are yellow, both are pressable, money, or the player.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Stocks Rule",
        "body": "Every surface is box black or map paper. There is no third gray panel; a surface that is neither is a device (pager, radio) and is drawn as a black object.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Embossed Logo Rule",
        "body": "Display type is italic, expanded and heavy, or it is not display type. Its depth is a stepped hard extrusion in silver (logo) or ink (banners), the printed emboss of a box front.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every number on screen is Barlow Condensed with tabular numerals, so cash, ammo and timers never jitter.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Clear Windscreen Rule",
        "body": "HUD never covers the play area's centre. New HUD pieces take a corner or an edge slot, and on phones they queue for a shared slot rather than stack.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Printed, Not Lit Rule",
        "body": "No glow, no blur, no glass, no gradients standing in for light. A shadow says \"this object lies on top\"; it never says \"this emits\".",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Off-Square Rule",
        "body": "Stickers and roundels sit a little rotated (-9deg to 8deg); manual pages and map print sit true. Rotation marks something stuck on, not printed in.",
        "section": "shapes"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Map Key Rule",
        "body": "A map ink means the same thing in the manual, the HUD and the city: yellow is the payphone and money, red is the target and damage, blue is the garage.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** print every surface on box black or map paper, outlined in ink (#14130f).",
      "**Do** set display type in Archivo italic, heavy and expanded, and give it a stepped hard extrusion when it is a logo or banner.",
      "**Do** use hazard yellow only for what is pressable, money, or the player.",
      "**Do** slap stickers on with a fast scale-down and slight rotation on the exponential ease-out (cubic-bezier(.16, 1, .3, 1)).",
      "**Do** give every new feature a touch key, and keep HUD pieces in corner or edge slots.",
      "**Do** keep map inks consistent between the manual's key, the HUD and the canvas."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use dark glass panels, backdrop blur, glow, scanlines, CRT curvature or emoji.",
      "**Don't** loop animation for decoration; banners slam once, LEDs blink a set count and stop.",
      "**Don't** introduce a second accent colour or a gray card surface.",
      "**Don't** use pixel or terminal fonts (Press Start 2P, VT323) or a system display face.",
      "**Don't** use distinctive names from the series this parodies; parody names only."
    ]
